  "decision_needed": [
    {
      "question": "Rural fire reimbursement 23,194 is printed under Other Financing Sources in the governmental funds statement (p6) but as a general revenue in the Statement of Activities (p3) and an operating receipt in the budget schedule (p9). Should it count as a receipt?",
      "amount": 23194,
      "recorded_as": "other_financing (as printed in the governmental funds statement)",
      "source_page": 6
    },
    {
      "question": "General Fund 'Other receipts' 1,558,567 (Total 1,564,034; Statement of Activities 'Miscellaneous') is most of the year's governmental receipts and is not explained in the trimmed pages; the General Fund then transferred 2,353,066 out (mostly to the Road Fund for capital outlay). Is it a grant, loan/bond proceeds, or a sale?",
      "amount": 1564034,
      "recorded_as": "receipt category other",
      "source_page": 5
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Modified cash basis audit (basis recorded as cash). Governmental lines from the Statement of Revenues, Expenditures, and Changes in Fund Balances (Total Governmental Funds, pp5-6; funds General, Road, Debt Service; the p4 balance sheet calls the Road Fund 'Street Fund'). Fund balance roll-forward: 1,846,169 + 2,043,393 - 1,380,472 + 23,194 + 2,378,466 - 2,421,466 = 2,489,284. Transfers in/out are the printed Total-column figures; the 43,000 difference went to the Water Fund. Cash from the governmental funds statement (p4): 2022 cash 2,337,256 + county treasurer 6,508 = 2,343,764, certificates of deposit 145,520 as investments; 2021 column: cash 495,154 + county treasurer 6,076, investments = certificates of deposit 144,939 + Investments 1,200,000. Business-type (Water, Sewer) lines from the modified cash proprietary statement (p8), which ties to the Statement of Activities (expenses 1,225,826, charges 202,582, capital grants 2,672,918, investment income 16, transfers 43,000); net position 1,920,299 -> 3,612,989 (no restatement in FY2022). Water grants recorded as state aid: the all-funds budgetary comparison (p9) prints the capital grants as 'Intergovernmental: State grants and shared revenues'. Balance sheet = government-wide Statement of Net Position (includes capital assets and debt, so not the funds statement). Detail = per-fund columns of the governmental funds and proprietary funds statements; the only supplementary schedule is the all-funds budgetary comparison (pp9-10), not used to avoid double counting. Read pages 1-10 of 10"
}
